{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:99595",
  "title": "Moderate: rpm security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-13 12:06:37"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-24 12:08:02"
  },
  "severity": "Moderate",
  "description": "The RPM Package Manager (RPM) is a command-line driven package management system capable of installing, uninstalling, verifying, querying, and updating software packages.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* rpm: Command injection in rpmuncompress via unescaped filenames passed to popen() (CVE-2026-84838)\n\n* rpm: Command Injection in `rpmbuild -t*` (`getTarSpec`) via Unescaped Tarball Path (CVE-2026-84837)\n\n* rpm: Command Execution via Macro Expansion in `rpmuncompress -x` for Crafted `.gem` Filenames (CVE-2026-84233)\n\n* rpm: rpmbuild getTarSpec() crafted tar member name ? macro injection (CVE-2026-78367)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
